From 728653cbc2a8280a40e233d7893d3249f93863aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] emscripten: same-instance fork under Shiro
 (BLINK_SAME_INSTANCE_FORK=1)

With the flag, fork() and clone() without CLONE_VM make the child a new
System with its own guest thread in this Blink instance, in the same wasm
memory, instead of a snapshot restored in another worker (0014) or the
child running on the parent's thread (0023). Private pages are copied
(the 0014 snapshot, restored in place); the pages of writable MAP_SHARED
mappings, anonymous or kernel files, move onto host pages of their own
that both map (PTE bit PAGE_GROW, unused before; memorymalloc.c
refcounts them and the last unmapper frees one), so the memory and the
futexes in it are shared, and parent and child run concurrently under
the GIL.

The child's kernel calls go out as its pid. Its exit_group ends its
kernel process and its System; a fatal signal's default action kills it
through the kernel; an exec starts the new program in a worker of its own
(the kernel's embryo exec) and the System goes. shiro_hosted() tells the
page, which routes the child's signals to it by pid
(blink_shiro_signal_pid), turns its kernel termination (kill -9) into a
SIGKILL for its System, and keeps the worker until the last process in it
ends: a parent that exits with children running reports its exit and
ends only its own thread.

Known limits: a multi-threaded child's other threads aren't reaped on its
exit; pages of host blocks moved onto shared pages stay with their block.
